  "reason": "The records collectively establish that milling time can refine HEA microstructures, increase hardness, accumulate processing-related defects, and promote solid-solution formation, while also identifying grain refinement, dislocation density, and solid-solution strengthening as relevant mechanisms. They also show that thermal processing or sintering controls phase stability and that melting point can influence the sequence of elemental dissolution. However, none describes the specific Co-Cr-Fe-Ni-Ti system processed by short-duration HEBM followed by vacuum SPS, nor do they predict the stabilized 83% FCC/17% BCC mixture. Thus they point strongly in the right direction, but selecting SPS and the particular processing window and phase outcome would still require a substantial new idea."
